From 52d2d48d01025f21a7010901bae31a49c86acac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meng-amd <limitmhw@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Quantization] Support native Quark W4A16 INT4/UINT4 exports
 (#48606)

Version-locked to VLLM_REF=v0.29.0. Upstream PR #48606
(https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48606) open as of 2026-09-10,
not in any tag. Pinned to head 52d2d48 (branch
hongweimeng/quark-awq-int4-quark-flow_experiment, 9 files, +1128/-6).
Drop when VLLM_REF contains the merge — and confirm ROCm/gfx1201 kernel
coverage, not just the merge: the dense QuarkW4A16Int4 path selects an
MPLinearKernel at load time (ROCm order: RDNA3/gfx1100-only, then
RDNAHybrid gfx11/gfx12, then TritonW4A16 fallback), so gfx1201 support is
unproven until the AWQ trial boots.

Ported to v0.29.0 (the PR base drifted; 4 files needed rebase):
- quark/quark.py: `_is_w4a16_int4` adapted to the v0.29.0 bool-checker
  style; dispatch added to `_get_scheme_from_config` (replaces the PR's
  `_get_scheme_cls_from_config`/`init_scheme` split, which does not exist
  on v0.29.0); `_unwrap_single_quant_config` ported from main (absent on
  v0.29.0). The PR's `weight_config=`/`layer_name=` get_scheme hunks are
  N/A — v0.29.0 resolves configs via `_find_matched_config` and already
  passes `layer_name`.
- quark/quark_moe.py: `QuarkW4A16Int4MoEMethod` ported to the v0.29.0 MoE
  API (`super().__init__(moe)`; dispatch via the `get_moe_method`
  staticmethod checker chain instead of the PR's `get_moe_method_target`,
  which does not exist on v0.29.0). Oracle calls
  (`select/convert/make_wna16_*`) verified against v0.29.0 signatures.
- tests/quantization/test_quark.py hunks DROPPED (test-only; the image
  build does not run them).
- schemes/quark_w4a16_int4.py: `super().__init__(keys)` replaced with plain
  attribute assignment — v0.29.0's QuarkScheme is a bare ABC with no
  __init__ (the PR-base call raises `TypeError` at load time); added the
  required `has_g_idx=False` to `MPLinearLayerConfig(...)` (field absent
  on the PR base).
All other hunks (new `schemes/quark_w4a16_int4.py`, schemes `__init__`,
kernels/linear log line, triton_moe, auto_awq) applied cleanly unmodified.
NOTE to future editors: this file is applied with `git apply`, which
silently truncates a hunk body that exceeds its `@@` line count — always
update the counts when adding/removing `+` lines (2026-09-10: a stale
+1,217 dropped the file tail and crash-looped the server at import).
